  "notes": "Cash basis. Governmental lines from the Total column of the governmental funds statement (p4); interest income, bond proceeds and bond payments are printed under Other Financing Sources (Uses): bond proceeds 205,800 in debt_proceeds, the rest in other_financing. Governmental roll-forward on fund balance (1,091,436 -> 368,474); beginning cash not printed; ending_cash = governmental funds total assets (cash 364,846 + county treasurer 3,628, p3). Business-type from proprietary statement p6 (Total column, cash basis; its title misprints 'Year ended September 30, 2021' but figures match the 2022 columns on p11); interest, property tax for water bond, bond payments and capital outlay are below its totals under Other Receipts (Disbursements) (outside_printed_total). Proprietary cash flows p7-p8. Detail: per fund column of p4 (General, Street, Keno) and per fund from the proprietary schedule p11 2022 columns (Water, Sewer, Sanitation). The p10 General Fund statement equals the governmental Total column and the p9 budget schedule is a combined all-funds schedule, so neither is recorded (no double counting), as in FY2023. Governmental capital outlay statement line spans General and Street, so no function in its label. Statement of Activities is cash basis, so governmental_net_position null. Several 1-dollar rounding gaps in the report (report_discrepancies). Read pages 1-11 of 11"
